[sho@maxwell.physics.purdue.edu (Sho Kuwamoto) writes:]
[]Case in point: You kill a leather golem, it turns into a couple suits
[]of leather armor.  Why?

ummm, perhaps the monster is (somehow) carrying those items and not
really turning into them, which is how it might appear during play.
perhaps, the leather armor is possibly super-enchanted (say +9 or so).
i've never seen this but someone said that they did ...

it makes sense in an abstract way that a dragon corpse turns into
armor via polymorph. however, it is my gut feeling that the vast
majority of hackers (who don't subscribe to r.g.h) will never discover
this feature because it is _too_ abstract and circumstantial and you
can't wish for it if you've never heard of it (unlike precious gems
in early versions of hack).

you could leave the polymorph-corpse-into-armor feature in the game,
it doesn't hurt, but there ought to be a clue (i.e. a 1% chance that
a dragon kill leaves a corpse and armor, that the dragon was carrying).
dragons would instinctively only carry (protect) armor of their kind.

